.TH MODBUS-CACHE-CTL 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-cache-ctl \- one-shot control client for the modbus-cache daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-cache-ctl
.RI [ options ]
.IB command " [args ...]"
.br
.B modbus-cache-ctl
.RI [ options ]
< commands

.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends one control command (or a batch piped on stdin, one per line) to the
\fBmodbus-cache\fR JSON-lines control server and prints the replies on
stdout, one per line. Every invocation lands in the audit trail (prefix
\fBCTL\fR).
.PP
The command grammar is the daemon's: \fBset\fR/\fBunset\fR/\fBshow\fR/
\fBhelp\fR (the settings registry), \fBinspect\fR, \fBshow status\fR,
\fBshow connections\fR, \fBshow cache\fR [\fBall\fR], \fBshow uplink\fR,
\fBshow version\fR, \fBshow knobs\fR (the dictionary of the registry),
\fBclear cache\fR, \fBrestart\fR, \fBshutdown\fR,
\fBquit\fR. See
.BR modbus-cache (1)
CONTROL.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (default: /tmp/modbus\-cache\-15502.socket; env CTL when
unset) — same flag as the proxy itself
.TP
.B command
control command, e.g. inspect, show status, show cache, clear cache,
restart, shutdown
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds (default 5.0)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env CONTROL_TOKEN); a file:<path> value
reads the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout; default: the XDG state home
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size, 0 = off (default: 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail (default: off)


.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-cache-ctl show status
.IP \(bu 2
.B modbus-cache-ctl clear cache
.IP \(bu 2
.B printf 'show cache\\nclear cache\\n' | modbus-cache-ctl
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every command answered \fBok\fR.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-cache (1),
.BR modbus-cache-cli (1)
